{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-23 09:51:19 UTC] [Agent: ArchitectAgent-DocUpdate] [Project: documentation_update] Architectural decision: Phased approach by priority (HIGH->MEDIUM->LOW) rather than by document type. Rationale: HIGH priority docs (README, AGENTS_EXTENDED, CLAUDE.md) have widest user impact and establish the v2.2 baseline language that later phases reference. Sequential execution required to maintain consistency. | alternatives_rejected=[\"document_type_grouping\", \"parallel_execution\"]; decision=priority_based_phasing; reasoning={\"how\": \"Priority-based phasing ensures each document is fully updated once, and earlier phases establish patterns for later phases\", \"what\": \"Alternative was by-document-type (all version bumps first, then new sections). Rejected because it would require revisiting files multiple times and risks inconsistent baseline language.\", \"why\": \"Need to choose execution order that maximizes impact and maintains consistency\"}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/documentation_update/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-23T09:51:19.293125+00:00_f812fbda", "timestamp": "2026-01-23T09:51:19.293177+00:00"}
